/**
	Splits a value into its whole number and fractional parts.
	1. double modf(double num, double&out iptr);
	2. float modf(float num, float&out iptr);
	## Arguments:
		* double/float num: the value to split.
		* double/float&out iptr: a variable that receives the whole number part of the value.
	## Returns:
		double/float: the fractional part of the value.
	## Remarks:
		Both parts keep the sign of the original value, so splitting -3.75 gives a fractional part of -0.75 and a whole number part of -3.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	double whole;
	double fraction = modf(3.75, whole);
	alert("Example", "3.75 has a whole number part of " + whole + " and a fractional part of " + fraction);
}
